<title>USA: Synovus Financial Corp Q3 shr up to $0.30.</title>
<headline>Synovus Financial Corp Q3 shr up to $0.30.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ga. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.30		    $0.26</p>
<p> Net			 35,208		   30,279</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 116,295		  115,398</p>
<p>	   9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.84		    $0.71</p>
<p> Net			 97,943		   80,949</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 116,066		  114,662</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q3 and nine month net includes SAIF assessment of after-tax $2.8 million, or $0.024 a share.</p>
<p>Q3 net interest income $95.6 million vs $86.3 million.</p>
<p>Q3 provision for loan losses $8.0 million vs $6.2 million.</p>
<p>Nine month net interest income $277.4 million vs $253.6 million.</p>
<p>Nine month provision for loan losses $22.7 million vs $17.2 million.</p>
<p>Total assets at Sept 30 $8.34 billion vs $7.62 billion.</p>
<p>Net loans at Sept 30 $5.85 billion vs $5.37 billion.</p>
<p>Total deposits at Sept 30 $6.88 billion vs $6.46 billion.</p>
